{# Google Material Symbols, inlined as SVG rather than loaded as the icon font.

   Inline keeps the properties the hand-drawn set had: the glyph inherits
   currentColor, costs no extra request, and cannot flash a blank box while a
   font loads. Pulling the font from Google Fonts instead would put a
   render-blocking third-party request on every page and send every reader to
   Google, on a site that otherwise self-hosts everything it serves.

   Paths are Google's own, taken unmodified from the Material Symbols
   Outlined set (Apache 2.0). They use Material's own 0 -960 960 960 viewBox,
   which is why these differ from the 0 0 24 24 set they replaced; .icon sizes
   in em, so the coordinate system does not matter.

   All are decorative - the adjacent text carries the meaning - hence
   aria-hidden. #}

{# star, fill1: the filled variant on purpose. The outlined star is too faint
   to read as a mark against a stop's name at 0.85em. #}
{% macro icon_star() -%}
<svg class="icon icon--star" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m233-120 65-281L80-590l288-25 112-265 112 265 288 25-218 189 65 281-247-149-247 149Z"/></svg>
{%- endmacro %}

